    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "Colgan Air's plane could push its own nose down.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 3.21,
        "window": 3.8,
        "fill": 0.845
      },
      {
        "scene": "how",
        "text": "So why didn't it save the plane? The control column shakes first, as a warning. If the wing gets close to losing its lift, a machine shoves the column forward.",
        "start": 4.1,
        "seconds": 10.1,
        "window": 10.77,
        "fill": 0.938
      },
      {
        "scene": "night",
        "text": "Near Buffalo, in February 2009, the shaker fired at 131 knots. Then the pusher fired. So why did the nose come back up?",
        "start": 14.87,
        "seconds": 9.92,
        "window": 10.6,
        "fill": 0.936
      },
      {
        "scene": "fight",
        "text": "But the captain dragged the column back against it. It fired twice more, and he pulled back each time.",
        "start": 25.47,
        "seconds": 6.15,
        "window": 6.8,
        "fill": 0.904
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "The airliner rolled hard onto its right side, dived, and hit a house. All 49 aboard were killed, and 1 on the ground.",
        "start": 34.6,
        "seconds": 7.99,
        "window": 8.63,
        "fill": 0.926
      },
      {
        "scene": "loop",
        "text": "Machine or pilot: who gets the last word? Full story on our channel.",
        "start": 43.23,
